"quoi": "Verona collected waste in open containers while neighbouring municipalities operate door-to-door collection, which attracted a \"migration\" of waste (nearly 20 % of fines targeted non-residents). The new system, rolled out progressively by the AMIA utility, now covers more than half the municipal territory: badge-operated containers for residual and organic waste, door-to-door collection for paper and plastics-metals. Objective: a 65 % sorting rate in order to stop paying the regional surcharge on residual waste. A city of 250,000 inhabitants, comparable to a large Brussels municipality.",
