"quoi": "Munich's \"Zweckentfremdung\" regulation prohibits leaving a dwelling empty or diverting it to tourist letting or office use without authorisation. 2025 assessment: 507 dwellings brought back to residential use (448 in 2024), of which 254 were vacant, 145 let to tourists and 108 used commercially, that is around 30,000 m²; coercive penalty payments of 1.2 M€ and fines of more than 700,000 € (290,768 € in 2024); 1,225 reports from citizens via the online platform. Since 1 August 2026, the revised regulation allows investigators to request, case by case, the energy consumption data of a suspect dwelling; prior registration of short-term lettings becomes compulsory. The Sozialreferat rejects the vacancy tax of 20 € per m² per month proposed by Die Linke: \"we want to put an end to vacancy, not create new taxes\".",
